Use <natural units>, the <Minkowski metric> $g=\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1)$ and the <Feynman i-epsilon prescription>. In question 1 use <dimensional regularization> with $d=4-2\epsilon$ and write $C_\epsilon=1/(16\pi^2\epsilon)$; in the alternative convention $d=4-\epsilon$, replace $C_\epsilon$ by $1/(8\pi^2\epsilon)$. Only <ultraviolet poles> are retained there. Figure 1 is unreadable in the released source: the corresponding specific gaps are marked below. All other parts have complete derivations.

